<title>SINGAPORE: APB half year net profit up 14.4 pct.</title>
<headline>APB half year net profit up 14.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   49.46	vs	43.23</p>
<p>Dividend (cts)		9.00	vs	 9.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	  19.50	vs	17.10</p>
<p>    Turnover		    753.45	vs     694.60</p>
<p>    Other income		 14.31	vs	 9.38</p>
<p>    Interest expense	    7.89	vs	 4.50</p>
<p>    Investment income	   1.47	vs	 1.18</p>
<p>    Tax			    31.14	vs	23.62</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		92.76	vs	78.24</p>
<p>    Dividend register/pay    July 8/July 18</p>
<p>Note - Asia Pacific Breweries is a joint venture between</p>
<p>Fraser &amp; Neave Ltd and Heineken NV.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
